{"answer":"The web UI uses one WebSocket per browser tab, served by lore-api at `/api/ws` (the URL is set by `LORE_WS_URL`, formerly `LORE_PLANS_WS_URL`). It carries JSON text frames with client-chosen channel ids and multiplexes named channels. The `run` channel forwards an assembly run's pod events and transcript. It is authorized by a token minted through POST /api/assembly-runs/{id}/stream-token. The `plan` channel tunnels the plan editor's Hocuspocus collaboration bytes to the same collaboration server, and the collab-token handshake stays inside the tunnel. The web-ui keeps the socket in a provider above every page, so navigating from a plan to its run keeps the connection. This replaced the earlier SSE stream (ADR-037) under ADR-048 (PR #2122). The row-id cursor, the catch-up-then-live semantics and the Postgres NOTIFY fan-out are unchanged. On the server, there is one feed per run.","sources":["adrs/ADR-048-one-websocket-for-live-channels.md","adrs/ADR-037-sse-run-observability.md","pull-2122","session-summary/2026-09-23-one-live-socket"]}
```

